 null, 'The Bohr effect describes how increased carbon dioxide and decreased pH (increased acidity), as seen in actively metabolizing tissues, reduce hemoglobin''s affinity for oxygen, promoting oxygen release.'),
('NEET PG', 'Pre- and Para-Clinical Sciences', 'Physiology', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'The baroreceptor reflex, involving receptors in the carotid sinus and aortic arch, primarily helps regulate:',
 '[{"text":"Blood glucose levels","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Blood pressure","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Body temperature","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Respiratory rate alone","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Baroreceptors in the carotid sinus and aortic arch detect changes in blood pressure and trigger reflex adjustments in heart rate and vascular tone to maintain stable blood pressure.'),
('NEET PG', 'Pre- and Para-Clinical Sciences', 'Physiology', 'easy', 'mcq',
 'Which reflex helps protect the airway by closing the epiglottis during swallowing?',
